    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0871" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg761"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3, 1890</date>.
                        (Received May 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 123.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of my note to the Porte
                    about Moussa Bey, referred to at the close of my No. 113 of 18th ultimo. In this
                    note I have endeavored to answer the points advanced by the minister of justice,
                    on <pb facs="0872" n="762" xml:id="pg762"/> whose report the minister of foreign
                    affairs based his note. I did not dwell at any length on the “ordonnance de non
                    lieu,” because I was unable to find the date of it, which I am yet trying to
                    obtain.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d470-a1.xml" xpointer="d470-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
